{"about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">\u201cChymicalia - Change is Possible!\u201d</h2><br>So reads the glowing sign outside the suspicious door that just appeared out of nowhere between two boarded-up buildings on the rough side of town.<br><br>An ordinary Yorkshire town, like any other... but not for long.<br><br>Because Chymicalia is a sentient alchemy shop, roving across the cosmos, trapping one poor soul after another as its unwilling servant.<br><br>For the last ten years, that servant has been you.<br><br>But now you\u2019re here, back in the town you thought you'd never see again, and maybe somehow, this time, things are going to change. <br><br><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2287720/extras/3elixirs_256_frame.gif?t=1745760582\" /><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Make potions! Make friends! Make terrible mistakes!</h2><br>Chymicalia is an alchemy sim with a choice-driven narrative, where you talk to customers, listen to their troubles and attempt to create a potion that will solve their problems. Or at least, give them different problems.<br><br>However, Chymicalia is a sentient shop, with its own sinister agenda for its customers. Keeping everyone satisfied isn't going to be easy.<br><br>Is change really possible, in this hopeless town? Can you really help any of these people change their lives?<br><br>And even if you do... who\u2019s going to help you change yours?","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2287720?t=1745760582","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2287720/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1745760582","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2287720/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1745760582","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2287720/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1745760582","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Steam Achievements","id":22},{"description":"Captions available","id":13},{"description":"Partial Controller Support","id":18},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\">\u201cChymicalia - Change is Possible!\u201d</h2><br>So reads the glowing sign outside the suspicious door that just appeared out of nowhere between two boarded-up buildings on the rough side of town.<br><br>An ordinary Yorkshire town, like any other... but not for long.<br><br>Because Chymicalia is a sentient alchemy shop, roving across the cosmos, trapping one poor soul after another as its unwilling servant.<br><br>For the last ten years, that servant has been you.<br><br>But now you\u2019re here, back in the town you thought you'd never see again, and maybe somehow, this time, things are going to change. <br><br><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2287720/extras/3elixirs_256_frame.gif?t=1745760582\" /><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Make potions! Make friends! Make terrible mistakes!</h2><br>Chymicalia is an alchemy sim with a choice-driven narrative, where you talk to customers, listen to their troubles and attempt to create a potion that will solve their problems. Or at least, give them different problems.<br><br>However, Chymicalia is a sentient shop, with its own sinister agenda for its customers. Keeping everyone satisfied isn't going to be easy.<br><br>Is change really possible, in this hopeless town? Can you really help any of these people change their lives?<br><br>And even if you do... who\u2019s going to help you change yours?","developers":["Falling Awkwardly"],"genres":[{"description":"Indie","id":"23"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2287720/header.jpg?t=1745760582","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><strong>OS:</strong> Tested on